# skeepto WASM → build/

The user serves/tests the app from `skeepto/build/`, not `public/` directly.

After `compil2Wasm.sh` (or any WASM rebuild in `sker/`), artifacts land in `skeepto/public/`. The user serves from `build/` — **remind them** to sync; do not run sync yourself unless they ask (see `user-compiles.mdc`).

Full sync:

```bash
cd /Users/stephaneallez/Projects/skeepto && npm run build
```

WASM-only:

```bash
cp public/SkReactSpreadSheet.{mjs,wasm,wasm.map} build/
cp public/SkReactSpreadSheet.{mjs,wasm,wasm.map} Node/Server/
```

Remind hard-refresh (**Cmd+Shift+R**) so the browser reloads `.wasm`.
